  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The $4\\times4$ grid below is formed of unit squares.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-grid",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 13, p13-q8-grid\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.25pt,step=1] (0,0) grid (4,4);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (4,4);\n\\node[black,anchor=south east,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (0,4) {$A$};\n\\node[black,anchor=north west,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (4,0) {$B$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 40,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 13,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 8, upper left column",
          "description": "Four-by-four unshaded unit-square grid. Native TikZ is used because the blank-grid template does not provide the required corner labels A and B.",
          "mathematics": "A is the top-left vertex; B is the bottom-right vertex. The centre is the unmarked intersection two units right and two units down from A.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only the supplied grid and corner labels are visible; no paths or centre marker are supplied."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By travelling only right (R) and down (D), how many paths are there from $A$ to $B$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$70$",
          "worked": "Each path contains four R steps and four D steps. These are arrangements of eight objects with two groups of four identical objects.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nN&=\\frac{8!}{4!4!}\\\\\nN&=70.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many of these paths pass through the centre of the grid?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$36$\n\nMultiply the numbers of paths to and from the centre.",
          "worked": "From $A$ to the centre, each path contains two R steps and two D steps. The same counts apply from the centre to $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nN_{\\text{each half}}&=\\frac{4!}{2!2!}\\\\\nN_{\\text{each half}}&=6\\\\\nN_{\\text{through centre}}&=6\\times6\\\\\nN_{\\text{through centre}}&=36.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
